---
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: AI training for agriculture and agrifood teams
metaTitle: "AI Workshops and Training for Agriculture & Agrifood | Dr. Maryna Kuzmenko"
description: "AI workshops, talks and custom courses for agriculture and agrifood teams, online or on site: AI literacy and AI fluency training by Dr. Maryna Kuzmenko."
---
{#
  Team training. Moved here from aiinagriculture.org/ai-training-agrifood/ on
  2026-10-24, at the same path, so the old address can point straight at it;
  aiinagriculture.org's "Workshops" page is now a short invite to this one.

  The formats, topics, law, figures and questions are read from
  src/_data/training.js — see it for the decisions that came across with the
  page. Nothing here is a price.
#}
{% from "partials/photo.njk" import photo %}
{% set enquiry = "/contact/?type=training" %}

<section class="hero hero--split">
  <div class="hero__text">
    <span class="eyebrow">Team training for agriculture and agrifood</span>
    <h1>AI fluency for the people who <span class="italic-text">grow, process and feed the world.</span></h1>
    <p class="lead">
      Practical AI literacy training for agricultural and agrifood organisations.
      From a one-hour lecture to a fully customised course, your team learns what
      AI can really do in the field, the lab and the supply chain, and how to use
      it with confidence.
    </p>
    <div class="hero__actions">
      <a class="btn btn--primary" href="{{ enquiry }}">Book a training session</a>
      <a class="btn btn--ghost" href="#topics">Explore topics</a>
    </div>
    <p class="training-trust">
      Delivered by me, Dr. Maryna Kuzmenko: agri-AI founder, researcher and
      educator. Online or on site, across the UK and internationally.
    </p>
  </div>
  {{ photo(photos.workshop, sizes="(max-width: 900px) 100vw, 520px", eager=true, class="hero__photo") }}
</section>

<ul class="stats training-glance" aria-label="At a glance">
  <li class="stat"><strong>45 min to 12 weeks</strong><span>From a keynote to a full course</span></li>
  <li class="stat"><strong>Online or on site</strong><span>Live, in person, or both at once</span></li>
  <li class="stat"><strong>5 to several hundred</strong><span>Workshops of up to 25 per group</span></li>
  <li class="stat"><strong>No coding needed</strong><span>Advanced tracks if you want them</span></li>
</ul>

<section class="section">
  <div class="training-split">
    <div>
      <span class="eyebrow">Why AI fluency, why now</span>
      <h2>AI is already in your sector. Is your team ready for it?</h2>
      <p>
        Computer vision counts fruit and measures leaves. Sensors and models
        predict yield, disease and milk output. Language tools draft reports,
        grant bids and supplier emails in seconds. Your competitors, customers
        and funders are already asking how you use AI.
      </p>
      <p>
        Yet most teams were never taught what AI actually is, where it works and
        where it fails. That gap leads to two costly mistakes: ignoring tools that
        could save hours every week, or buying expensive solutions that never fit
        the farm, the lab or the data.
      </p>
      <p class="pointer-box">{{ training.definition }}</p>
    </div>

    <ul class="training-benefits">
      <li><strong>Make better decisions</strong> about AI tools, vendors and pilots</li>
      <li><strong>Work faster</strong> with everyday AI assistants, safely and responsibly</li>
      <li><strong>Collect better data</strong> today, so AI projects succeed tomorrow</li>
      <li><strong>Speak the same language</strong> across agronomy, operations, R&amp;D and leadership</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section" style="border-top: 1px solid var(--border);">
  <span class="eyebrow">Who it is for</span>
  <h2>Built for agriculture and agrifood teams</h2>
  <div class="grid training-audiences">
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Farms and growers</h3>
      <p>Managers, agronomists and technical staff who want to use AI on the ground.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Food producers, packers and retailers</h3>
      <p>Operations, quality, supply chain and sustainability teams.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Agritech companies</h3>
      <p>Sales, product and customer success teams who need to explain AI clearly to farmers.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Research institutes and universities</h3>
      <p>Scientists, PhD students and technicians in plant science, phenotyping and animal science.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Industry bodies, cooperatives and advisers</h3>
      <p>Consultants, extension officers and member organisations.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Leadership teams and boards</h3>
      <p>Executives who need a clear, honest picture of AI's risks and opportunities.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p class="training-note">No coding or technical background is needed, unless you ask for an advanced track.</p>
</section>

<section class="section" id="formats" style="border-top: 1px solid var(--border);">
  <span class="eyebrow">Training formats</span>
  <h2>From a single talk to a full programme</h2>
  <p class="training-intro">Every format can be delivered online or in person, for groups of any size.</p>

  <table class="training-formats">
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th scope="col">Format</th>
        <th scope="col">Length</th>
        <th scope="col">Best for</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      {% for format in training.formats %}
      <tr>
        <th scope="row">{{ format.name }}</th>
        <td class="training-formats__length">{{ format.length }}</td>
        <td>{{ format.bestFor }}</td>
      </tr>
      {% endfor %}
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h3 class="training-addons__title">Add to any format</h3>
  <div class="badges">
    {% for addOn in training.addOns %}<span class="badge">{{ addOn }}</span>{% endfor %}
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section" id="topics" style="border-top: 1px solid var(--border);">
  <span class="eyebrow">Training topics</span>
  <h2>What your team can learn</h2>
  <p class="training-intro">
    Each topic works as a stand-alone lecture, a workshop or a module in a
    longer course. Mix and match them into your own programme.
  </p>

  <div class="speaking-topics-grid">
    {% for topic in training.topics %}
    <div class="topic-card">
      <div class="topic-icon" aria-hidden="true">{{ "0" + loop.index if loop.index < 10 else loop.index }}</div>
      <h3>{{ topic.title }}</h3>
      <p>{{ topic.summary }}</p>
    </div>
    {% endfor %}
    <div class="topic-card training-yours">
      <h3>Don't see your topic?</h3>
      <p>I can build a course around your own crop, livestock, product, process or research area.</p>
      <p><a class="text-link" href="{{ enquiry }}">Tell me what you need →</a></p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section" style="border-top: 1px solid var(--border);">
  <span class="eyebrow">How it works</span>
  <h2>From first email to confident team in four steps</h2>
  <ol class="training-steps">
    <li>
      <h3>Get in touch</h3>
      <p>
        Send a few lines through the <a class="inline-link" href="{{ enquiry }}">contact form</a>
        about your organisation, your team and what you would like to achieve.
      </p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <h3>Discovery call</h3>
      <p>
        A short call to understand your sector, your team's current AI skills
        and your goals, with an optional skills survey for participants.
      </p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <h3>Tailored proposal</h3>
      <p>
        A clear outline of the format, topics, schedule, delivery and price,
        with examples adapted to your crops, livestock, products or research.
      </p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <h3>Delivery and follow-up</h3>
      <p>
        Practical sessions online or on site, with materials your team keeps,
        and follow-up support to turn what they learned into action.
      </p>
    </li>
  </ol>
</section>

<section class="section" style="border-top: 1px solid var(--border);">
  <div class="training-split training-split--trainer">
    {{ photo(photos.bridgeAiTalk, sizes="(max-width: 900px) 100vw, 420px", class="page-figure--portrait") }}

    <div>
      <span class="eyebrow">About your trainer</span>
      <h2>Learn from someone who builds AI for agriculture</h2>
      <p>
        I'm a scientist, founder and educator working where AI meets agriculture,
        with nearly ten years of applying digital technology to farming. I
        co-founded Petiole, a UK agritech company that uses computer vision to
        measure plants in the field and the lab, and has won
        {{ facts.petiole.grants }} for practical AI in agriculture. I also founded
        MooMore, which uses AI thermal imaging to detect lameness early in dairy
        cattle.
      </p>
      <p>
        I turn complex technology into clear, practical language that farmers,
        food businesses and scientists can use straight away. I:
      </p>
      <ul class="speaking-list">
        <li>Host a {{ facts.live.name | lcfirst }} — <a class="inline-link" href="{{ facts.live.url }}">watch the recordings</a> ↗</li>
        <li>Write the {{ facts.newsletter.name }} for {{ facts.reach.newsletter }} readers — <a class="inline-link" href="{{ facts.newsletter.url }}">read the archive</a> ↗</li>
        <li>
          Created the course <a class="inline-link" href="{{ facts.links.course }}">{{ facts.course.title }}</a> ↗,
          taken by {{ facts.reach.students }} students in {{ facts.reach.countries }} countries
        </li>
        <li>Speak at industry events and give corporate keynotes — <a class="inline-link" href="/speaking/">speaking</a></li>
      </ul>

      <ul class="recognition-list training-credentials">
        <li><strong>{{ facts.award.wiw.name }}</strong> — {{ facts.award.wiw.status }}, for {{ facts.award.wiw.forLong }}.</li>
        <li><strong>{{ facts.award.ofc.name }}</strong> — {{ facts.award.ofc.selection }} in the cohort.</li>
        <li><strong>{{ facts.award.topVoice.name }}</strong> — named in {{ facts.award.topVoice.when }}.</li>
      </ul>

      <p>
        Because I build real AI systems for agriculture, every session is grounded
        in what actually works on farms and in labs, not in theory or sales talk.
        The full story is on the <a class="inline-link" href="/about/">About page</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{#
  Photographs of Maryna at work, in the order she gave them (2026-10-23).
  Columns rather than equal tiles, because cropping to one shape would cut the
